    "MicroTech II chiller",
    "ED 15063"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Chiller",
  "applies_to": "McQuay/Daikin Applied water-cooled centrifugal chillers with the MicroTech II unit controller and Modbus Communication Module: WSC, WDC, WPV, WMC (magnetic bearing), WCC, HSC/HDC heat recovery and TSC Templifier, per ED 15063-2 (Dec 2005).",
  "summary": "Older McQuay centrifugal chillers whose MicroTech II controller takes a plug-in Modbus RTU module. The map is a small fixed set of coils and 16-bit holding registers: start/stop, setpoints, water and refrigerant temperatures and pressures, flows, motor values for a selectable compressor, run hours and a 16-word alarm bitmap.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The document states that data element 1 is sent as index 0 in the PDU. Holding registers are printed in 4xxxx form (Cool Setpoint 40002 = wire address 1) and coils as plain element numbers (Chiller Enable coil 2 = wire address 1). The point tags confirm it: Active Setpoint 40003 is tagged A2 and Chiller Enable coil 2 is tagged D1."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "MicroTech II Chiller Unit Controller Protocol Information, Modbus Protocol",
    "doc_number": "ED 15063-2",
    "revision_date": "2005-12",
    "url": "https://tahoeweb.daikinapplied.com/api/general/DownloadDocumentByName/media/ED15063-2.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 7 (index rule), pp. 9-10 (data point summary), p. 11 (Table 2 model matrix), pp. 12-22 (point details), pp. 22-25 (Table 3 alarm bits)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Every analog value is one 16-bit holding register in English units (°F, psi gauge, gpm). 'x 10' in the units column means the value is sent times ten, so the scale is 0.1. Temperatures and pressures have signed ranges (for example -40 to 244 °F, -3276.8 to 3276.7 psi) and are typed INT16; counters and percentages are UINT16.",
    "Compressor Run Hours (40175) is printed as 'hours/10' with the note that the returned value must be multiplied by 10.",
    "Per-compressor registers (40015-40036, 40174, 40175) return the compressor chosen in Compressor Select (40161); pump run hours return the pump chosen with Pump Select (coil 20). Write the selector first, then read.",
    "Left out: Chiller Mode Output, printed as data type 'Coil' with index 40148 (type and index disagree), and Oil Feed Pressure 40033, printed 'psi' without the 'x 10' that every other pressure carries.",
    "Coil 3 is printed for both 'Chiller On Off' and 'Run Enabled' (both tagged D2); it is listed once.",
    "Active Alarms: 16 holding registers 40130-40145, one bit per alarm (Table 3 assigns no alarm to 40145, so it is not listed). Alarm n sits in register 40130 + n div 16, bit n mod 16 (alarm 1 = 40130 bit 1, alarm 16 = 40131 bit 0), as printed in Table 3. Which alarms a model raises varies by model, circuit count and options (Table 3 footnotes); the bit names here are not filtered by model.",
    "The unit's protocol, Modbus ID number (1-247) and baud rate are set at the keypad; the companion manual IM 743-1, MicroTech II Chiller Unit Controller Modbus Communication Module (May 2005, https://tahoeweb.daikinapplied.com/api/general/DownloadDocumentByName/media/IM743-1.pdf), covers module installation and those settings but gives no default baud rate.",
    "Liquid Line Refrigerant Pressure (40039) and Outdoor Air Temperature (40040) are not marked for the centrifugal models in Table 2 and are left out of this file. Oil points are not on WMC (magnetic bearing).",
    "Serial format is fixed at 8 data bits, no parity, 1 or 2 stop bits, 1200-19200 bps, RTU only (p. 6).",
    "Alarm 144 (Re-Start Fault Circuit 4) is printed with bit 0 but a blank register cell; it is placed in 40139 by the numbering rule."
  ],
